<title>BELGIUM: EU to investigate aid to France's SFP.</title>
<headline>EU to investigate aid to France's SFP.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission decided on Wednesday to begin an examination of French plans to 2.5 billion francs into loss-making SFP film studios.</p>
<p>In a statement the Commission said it had also given the green light for emergency aid of 350 million francs pending the start-up of a restructuring plan.</p>
<p>A small amount of the total 2.5 billion francs has already been granted to SFP -- the Societe Francaise de Production et de Creation Audiovisuelle.</p>
<p>Another 1.2 billion francs is intended to be a capital injection to pay for the restructuring and the rest will help reduce the company's debt.</p>
<p>The French government said late last year it planned to sell SFP, which produces live coverage of events for French television and also makes television and cinema films, to Generale des Eaux and Havas.</p>
</text>
